            # the backend form (`this.serverUrl`), a display value only. The
            # pattern carries the closing backtick and the semicolon, so it
            # matches a template literal that is the whole statement and not
            # an origin spliced into a larger in-Ingress URL.
            sub_filter 'window.location.origin}/`;' 'window.__WOOW_CANONICAL_URL__||window.location.origin}/`;';
            # Website share snippet (.s_share, .oe_share): the current page
            # address handed to Facebook, X, WhatsApp and the rest. This one
            # needs the path as well as the base, because under Ingress
            # location.href carries the Supervisor token and posting it to a
            # social network publishes it.
            #
            # The Ingress prefix is dropped whether or not a Canonical URL
            # exists -- this rule is the one exception to "no Canonical URL
            # means today's behaviour" (ADR 0006), because here today's
