            # broken as it was, but it no longer carries the token.
            sub_filter 'const currentUrl=window.location.href;' 'const currentUrl=(function(){var L=window.location,B=window.__WOOW_CANONICAL_URL__||L.origin,P="$safe_ingress_path",p=L.pathname;if(P&&p.indexOf(P)===0)p=p.slice(P.length)||"/";return B+p+L.search+L.hash})();';
            # The two places the web client navigates the whole frame to a
            # server-supplied URL (issue #174, U-E4). Both write `location`,
            # which the Runtime shim cannot wrap (ADR 0004), with a URL that
            # arrives over RPC and so is nowhere in the bundle for a prefix
            # rule to find. Under Ingress the frame leaves for the Home
            # Assistant root and Home Assistant answers 404: a Prefix escape
            # that loses the file and the screen with it.
            #
            # Each rewrite hands the value to __WOOW_INGRESS_URL__, the
            # helper the Runtime shim publishes, so the prefixing stays the
            # shim's own path() and not a copy of it. The identity fallback
            # keeps the expression total: an Ingress page whose shim did not
