            # The website editor's Blocks panel (issue #170, U-D2). Odoo 18
            # inlines OWL templates into the bundle as `registerTemplate(...)`
            # template literals, appended unminified after the JavaScript, so
            # each tile's own markup is served through this location:
            #   <div class="oe_snippet_thumbnail_img"
            #        t-attf-style="background-image: url({{snippet.thumbnailSrc}});"/>
            # A `url(` inside a style attribute is one of the ways the Runtime
            # shim does not wrap by decision (ADR 0004's 2026-09-28 postscript,
            # #169), and the `url(/` rules at the top of this location cannot
            # reach it either: the byte after `url(` here is `{`.
            #
            # The rewrite goes where the URL is *rendered* and not where it is
            # delivered, because this value round-trips to the database. The
            # editor's "Save block" hands `thumbnailSrc` -- the raw
            # `data-oe-thumbnail` of the snippet catalogue response -- to
            # `ir.ui.view.save_snippet` as `thumbnail_url`, which writes it into
            # the new snippet view's arch as `t-thumbnail`. Prefixing the
            # response would store the Ingress prefix, Supervisor token and all,
            # every time somebody saves a custom block under Ingress. So nothing
            # here touches `data-oe-thumbnail`, `render_public_asset` or
            # `save_snippet`, and a Static-tier test asserts that absence.
            #
            # The replacement has to stay valid in both skins it wears at once:
            # an XML attribute delimited by double quotes, inside a JavaScript
            # template literal. It therefore carries no double quote, no
            # backtick, no backslash and no `${`, and quotes with `'`, which is
            # why this one rule is written with a double-quoted parameter.
            # `+''` keeps the expression total: a value that is not a string
            # renders exactly as it does today instead of throwing in the tile.
            #
            # The protocol-relative limit of every other prefix rule is
            # inherited: `//host/path` starts with `/` and is prefixed like a
            # path. #166 fixes that for all of them at once or not at all. No
            # `t-thumbnail` Odoo ships is written that way.
            #
            # No double prefix. sub_filter never reads back what it wrote, so
            # the `$safe_ingress_path` this emits is not rescanned; `url(/` and
