            # of its own, keeping the entity exactly as it was. These belong
            # to the generic HTML location only -- asset bundles hold no HTML
            # entities -- and they are written by hand here, so the Rewrite
            # scan, which reads bundles, never learns about page HTML.
            #
            # They inherit the limit of the three above: the pattern is a
            # plain string, so a protocol-relative reference
            # (url(&#39;//cdn/x.png&#39;)) is prefixed too and breaks. No
            # sub_filter can express "root-relative but not //", and no
            # later rule can undo it, because nginx never rescans what a
            # rule replaced. Odoo writes none, and folding the rules into
            # something broader is a change to all seven (issue #166).
