            sub_filter 'url(&#34;/' 'url(&#34;$safe_ingress_path/';
            sub_filter 'url(&quot;/' 'url(&quot;$safe_ingress_path/';
            sub_filter 'url(&#x27;/' 'url(&#x27;$safe_ingress_path/';

            sub_filter '<head>' '<head>$ingress_runtime_shim';
        }

        # Action help HTML (issue #158, ADR 0004's 2026-09-28 postscript). A
        # window action's `help` field is HTML held in the database, and Odoo's
        # own help carries root-relative attributes -- the Surveys screen of an
        # empty list shows four `<img src="/survey/static/src/img/...">` sample
        # tiles. The web client reads that field out of this route's JSON-RPC
        # response and hands it to `markup()`, so it reaches the DOM as markup
        # (`innerHTML`) and never passes an API the Runtime shim wraps. Under
        # Ingress the four pictures were asked of the Home Assistant root and
        # answered 404: eight Prefix escapes per screen.
        #
        # The shim is not the fix. ADR 0004 records markup insertion as
        # uncovered *by decision*: the HTML editor and the website editor load
        # and save record content through that same path, so a shim hook would
        # write the Ingress prefix -- which carries the Ingress token -- back
        # into the database. Action help is only ever read through this
        # response and never saved through it, so a Literal rewrite scoped to
        # the route reaches it without reaching the editors.
        #
        # Inside JSON the attribute quote is escaped (`src=\"/survey/...`), so
        # the generic location's raw-quote HTML rules never matched a byte of
        # it; the only escaped-quote rules there cover `/web/assets/`, for the
        # Document Layout preview. Widening those to all JSON is what ADR 0004
        # calls unsafe -- 0.3.34 had to restrict the shim to `text/html` after
        # rewriting JSON blanked that preview -- so the new rules live in an
        # exact-match location of their own and no other JSON response sees
        # them.
        #
        # **This route and no other, even though three deliver help.** The web
        # client runs `markup(action.help)` over the answer of
        # `/web/action/load`, of `/web/action/run` and of
        # `/web/dataset/call_button/<model>/<method>` alike. Only the first is
        # safe to rewrite, and the difference is not the help: it is the rest
        # of the action dict.
        #
        # `/web/action/load` answers with a **stored** `ir.actions.act_window`
        # record. Its `help` is database HTML the client only ever displays,
        # and its `context` is the static string a developer wrote into the
        # action definition. Nothing in that response is content the client
        # will hand back.
        #
        # The other two answer with an action **computed at call time**, and a
        # computed action carries record content in its `context` as wizard
        # defaults. `marketing_card`'s `action_share()` button is the shipped
        # example: it returns an `act_window` whose
        # `context.default_body_arch` is a mail body holding
        # `<img src="/web/image/card.campaign/<id>/image_preview">` and
        # `<a href="/cards/<id>/preview">`. Prefix those and the mailing opens
        # pre-filled with the Ingress prefix, and the first save writes the
        # Supervisor token into `mailing.mailing.body_arch`. That is the
        # database-poisoning this entire decision exists to avoid, reached by
        # one more step. A server action's returned dict is user-authored
        # Python and is at least as open.
        #
        # So the rule is: **rewrite a response only when everything in it is
        # something the client displays and never returns.** Help delivered
        # through the other two routes keeps escaping, and that is the smaller
        # harm; it needs a fix that can tell a field from a field, which a
        # byte-level `sub_filter` cannot. `/web/action/load_breadcrumbs`
        # answers with display names only and needs nothing.
        #
        # Everything before `# Action help, escaped-quote rules` is every
        # directive of `location /` above, in its order and with only its
        # comments left behind: proxy headers, cookie path and flags,
        # X-Frame-Options removal, buffering, timeouts, and every rule it
        # carries. Ingress behaviour for this route differs from the generic
        # location only by the added rules, and `test_ingress_action_help.py`
        # compares the two directive lists, so later drift in either fails
        # rather than quietly changing the route.
        location = /web/action/load {
            proxy_pass http://odoo_http;
            proxy_http_version 1.1;
            proxy_set_header Host $http_host;
            proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
            proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Host $http_host;
            proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $ingress_proto;
            proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
            proxy_set_header Accept-Encoding "";
            proxy_hide_header X-Frame-Options;
            proxy_request_buffering off;
            proxy_buffering off;
            proxy_read_timeout 720s;
            proxy_send_timeout 720s;

            proxy_redirect ~^(?<odoo_redirect>/.*)$ $safe_ingress_path$odoo_redirect;
            proxy_cookie_path / $safe_ingress_path/;
            proxy_cookie_flags session_id $ingress_cookie_secure httponly samesite=lax;

            sub_filter_once off;
            sub_filter_types application/javascript text/javascript text/css application/json;
            sub_filter 'href="/' 'href="$safe_ingress_path/';
            sub_filter 'src="/' 'src="$safe_ingress_path/';
            sub_filter 'action="/' 'action="$safe_ingress_path/';
            sub_filter 'data-src="/' 'data-src="$safe_ingress_path/';
            sub_filter 'srcset="/' 'srcset="$safe_ingress_path/';
            sub_filter 'data-success-page="/' 'data-success-page="$safe_ingress_path/';
            sub_filter 'data-success_page="/' 'data-success_page="$safe_ingress_path/';
            sub_filter '.min.js"' '.min.js?woow_ingress=%%INGRESS_CACHE_VERSION%%"';
            sub_filter '.min.css"' '.min.css?woow_ingress=%%INGRESS_CACHE_VERSION%%"';
            sub_filter '&#39;/web/login&#39;' '&#39;$safe_ingress_path/web/login&#39;';
            sub_filter '"translationURL": "/website/' '"translationURL": "$safe_ingress_path/website/';
            sub_filter '"src": "/' '"src": "$safe_ingress_path/';
            sub_filter 'href=\\"/web/assets/' 'href=\\"$safe_ingress_path/web/assets/';
            sub_filter 'src=\\"/web/assets/' 'src=\\"$safe_ingress_path/web/assets/';
            sub_filter '"icon":"/' '"icon":"$safe_ingress_path/';
            sub_filter '"icon": "/' '"icon": "$safe_ingress_path/';
            sub_filter '"imgurl":"/' '"imgurl":"$safe_ingress_path/';
            sub_filter '"imgurl": "/' '"imgurl": "$safe_ingress_path/';
            sub_filter '/base/static/description/settings.png' '$safe_ingress_path/base/static/description/settings.png';
            sub_filter '`/web/webclient/' '`$safe_ingress_path/web/webclient/';
            sub_filter 'url(/' 'url($safe_ingress_path/';
            sub_filter "url('/" "url('$safe_ingress_path/";
            sub_filter 'url("/' 'url("$safe_ingress_path/';
            sub_filter 'url(&#39;/' 'url(&#39;$safe_ingress_path/';
            sub_filter 'url(&#34;/' 'url(&#34;$safe_ingress_path/';
            sub_filter 'url(&quot;/' 'url(&quot;$safe_ingress_path/';
            sub_filter 'url(&#x27;/' 'url(&#x27;$safe_ingress_path/';

            sub_filter '<head>' '<head>$ingress_runtime_shim';

            # Action help, escaped-quote rules, over the five URL attributes
            # the generic location's raw-quote rules cover. The two rules it
            # also carries for a website form's confirmation target
            # (`data-success-page`, and the pre-Odoo-14 `data-success_page`,
            # issue #167) get no escaped-quote counterpart: that value belongs
            # to page HTML, and a stored action's help never holds a form.
            #
            # The identity rules come first because they have to: sub_filter
            # settles two patterns that match at the same byte by the order
            # they are written, the earlier one winning even where a later one
            # is longer. Written ahead of the general rule, each identity rule
            # takes a URL that already carries the prefix and puts it back
            # unchanged, so nothing is prefixed twice. The escaped
            # `/web/assets/` rules above are ahead of both and keep answering
            # for the Document Layout preview, with the result the general
            # rules would have given anyway.
            #
            # Two limits are inherited from the raw-quote counterparts, because
            # a sub_filter pattern is a plain string and not a parser:
            #
            #   * a protocol-relative reference (`src=\"//cdn/x.png`) is
            #     prefixed too, and breaks;
            #   * `srcset` is a *list*, so only its first candidate is behind
            #     the attribute opener -- `srcset=\"/a 1x, /b 2x` prefixes
            #     `/a` and leaves `/b` escaping.
            #
            # Odoo's shipped action help writes neither shape, and both are
            # fixed for every such rule in this file at once or not at all
            # (issue #166).
            sub_filter 'href=\\"$safe_ingress_path/' 'href=\\"$safe_ingress_path/';
            sub_filter 'src=\\"$safe_ingress_path/' 'src=\\"$safe_ingress_path/';
            sub_filter 'action=\\"$safe_ingress_path/' 'action=\\"$safe_ingress_path/';
            sub_filter 'data-src=\\"$safe_ingress_path/' 'data-src=\\"$safe_ingress_path/';
            sub_filter 'srcset=\\"$safe_ingress_path/' 'srcset=\\"$safe_ingress_path/';
            sub_filter 'href=\\"/' 'href=\\"$safe_ingress_path/';
            sub_filter 'src=\\"/' 'src=\\"$safe_ingress_path/';
            sub_filter 'action=\\"/' 'action=\\"$safe_ingress_path/';
            sub_filter 'data-src=\\"/' 'data-src=\\"$safe_ingress_path/';
            sub_filter 'srcset=\\"/' 'srcset=\\"$safe_ingress_path/';
        }
    }
}
